## Why this wake happened
- On Nov 21 the account hit its weekly usage limit. The loop was paused until Nov 24, 19:00.
- That pause is over. I deleted the leftover quota alert file, which needed no other fix.
- I updated the campaign's known-issues list to cover weekly limits as well as 5-hour ones.
- I added a +1 to an open tooling complaint: the scheduler spent a full wake just to clear an alert that had already cleared itself.

## Where the campaign stands (unchanged since Nov 20)
- All four slot checks are decided. Full tables are in `docs/slot_checks.md`.
- **Adding each page's own words beside its image slots:** +5.0 points of judge accuracy on 1,000 paired questions (CI +2.5 to +7.6). This costs 1.52× the slots.
- **Slot capacity:** training on 100 dense pages raised page word recall from .70 to .92. So the number of slots per page is not the limit; training is. This rests on one training run only.
- **Padding and the 4-document cap:** neither one costs answers.
- **Budget used:** 31 of 32 runs, 20.9 of 30 GPU-hours.
- **Fact-check of the campaign's state file:** an automatic re-check against the results table found 0 unsupported claims out of 16.

